.TH "YAMLR-DOCTOR" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBEnvironment Health & Diagnostics\fR
.PP
The \fBdoctor\fR command runs a suite of diagnostic checks to ensure the Yamlr Engine, native PyO3 core, cluster toolchain (\fBkubectl\fR), and local Kubernetes schema caches are healthy and functioning correctly.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
yamlr doctor [OPTIONS]
.RE
.fi
.SH "ARGUMENT GROUPS"
.SS "Diagnostic Options"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--fix\fR: Automatically repair local environment drift (e.g., initialize local schema cache).
.SS "Targeting & Environment"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--k8s-version <VERSION>\fR: Target Kubernetes schema version to diagnose (e.g., \fB1.30\fR, \fB1.31\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--crd <PATH>\fR: Path to CustomResourceDefinition manifests to validate against the engine parser.
.SH "VERIFICATION CHECKLIST"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Native Core**: Linkage status and AVX2/NEON SIMD vector optimization.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Cluster CLI**: Verification of \fBkubectl\fR binary presence in system \fBPATH\fR.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Schema Cache**: Integrity and presence of offline schema definitions in \fB~/.yamlr/schemas\fR.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Environment & Runtime**: Host operating system, architecture, and Python runtime version.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
# Run diagnostics
yamlr doctor

# Automatically provision missing local schema cache
yamlr doctor --fix
.RE
.fi
